  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nA LONE NO-CONNECT PIN'S NET IS NAMED AFTER THE PIN (the export names it so, whatever label it carries), so the\none-pin net the text below names is, on this sheet: SPARE_GATE_OUT is 4Y.\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. The ASCII drawing in digital-and-supervision.md is a REPRESENTATION of this\nfile.\n\nALL SIX MODULE-END SPI PULLS ARE PLACED HERE (five R-SPI-PULL, and R-PULL-CS of R-CS-PULL-MOD). The row lives in interfaces/spi-link's bom.csv because that page\nderives the values, but the resistors are on the module board on both sides of this buffer, and the drawing\nabove shows both triples. Owning a row and placing an instance are different things; `of:` is what says so.\n\nThe cable-side CS pull is 100k to LOGIC_5V - see the bottom.\n\n[pins] WHICH SIGNAL GETS WHICH GATE IS ASSIGNED HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE [derived, not cited]. No page states it;\na netlist has to. Gate 4 is the spare the BOM row mentions. Contradict this in the page and the file follows.\n\n--- cable side: the three pulls that hold the BUFFER's inputs ------\n\n--- DAC side: the three that hold the DAC's inputs ----------------\n\nThese were bought for the state the cable-side three do not reach: module alive, instrument off, which is\nNORMAL and not a fault.\n\n[DIG_GND] THE FOUR ENABLES ARE TIED, NOT DRIVEN. OE_MOD is in hardware/nets.yaml's `retired:` section for\nexactly this reason: the comparator that gated it is not fitted, so there is no net crossing a boundary - just\nfour pins on the local ground.\n\n[4Y] THE SPARE GATE'S INPUT IS TIED, and it is tied because the BOM row says \"TIE EVERY UNUSED INPUT TO VCC OR\nGND\" - a floating CMOS input on an enabled gate is the one wrong answer. GND is chosen over VCC because the\npart has no input clamp to VCC and the ground tie cannot inject current into an unpowered rail. Its output\ndrives nothing, which is fine.\n\nTHE CABLE-SIDE CS PULL-UP, SETTLED 2026-09-30 (owner: 'Fix the SPI pull up'). CS_MOD has two pulls now, one at each end: R-CS-PULL-INST, 10k to 3V3 on the main board, where 3V3 exists, and R-PULL-CS here, 100k to LOGIC_5V. The strong one holds CS high while the ESP32 boots; the weak one holds it high with nothing plugged in, and is weak enough that a plugged-in, unpowered instrument sees ~45 uA into its dead 3V3 rail instead of 430 uA through its clamp. A pull-DOWN here was proposed and not fitted: the 74AHCT125 does not invert, so it would hold SYNC LOW - selected - whenever the umbilical is out. interfaces/spi-link/spi-link.md carries the three states." (at 256.54 38.099999999999994 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid cd626b92-20f2-58b8-b2aa-b31952beacda))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
